      "text": "$19^2-17^2+15^2-13^2+11^2-9^2+7^2-5^2+3^2-1^2=$\n$= (19^2-17^2)+(15^2-13^2)+(11^2-9^2)+(7^2-5^2)+(3^2-1^2)=$\n$= (19+17)(19-17)+(15+13)(15-13)+(11+9)(11-9)+(7+5)(7-5)+(3+1)(3-1)=\\boxed{200}$\n\nQuestion:\nMarine Stoney, a kohlrabi grower, harvested 19 pieces of kohlrabi last week and 23 pieces this week. If the wholesaler sold 38 pieces of kohlrabi yesterday and this morning, how many pieces are left for sale?\n\nThe total number of harvested kohlrabi is 19 + 23 = 42 pieces. The wholesaler sold 38 pieces yesterday afternoon and this morning. Therefore, the remaining pieces left for sale are 42 - 38 = 4 pieces. The answer is 4.\n\nOriginal Question:\nWhat is the side length in feet of a square whose area is 400 sq ft?\n$\n\\begin{gathered}\n  \\text{The area of a square} \\\\\\\\ \n  \\text{in square units} \\\\\\\\ \n  \\text{is length \\n times } \\\\\\\\\n    \\cdot \\text{length. \\\\\\\\ This is given by the formula} \\\\\\\\ \n  \\\\end{gathered}\n$\n\nGiven that the area of Polygon \\( ABCD \\) is \\( 400 \\, \\text{sq ft} \\):\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\text{Length} \\times \\text{Length}\n\\]\n\nLet the length of each side be \\( x \\). Then, the area of the square is:\n\n\\[\nx^2 = 400\n\\]\n\nTo find \\( x \\), we need to take the square root of 400:\n\n\\[\nx = \\sqrt{400}\n\\]\n\nLet's calculate this step-by-step using Python to ensure the accuracy of the result.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Given area of the square\narea = 400  # in square feet\n\n# Calculate the side length of the square\nside_length = math.sqrt(area)\nprint(side_length)\n```\n```output\n20.0\n```\nThe side length of the square is \\( \\boxed{20 \\, \\text{feet}} \\).",
